        "section": "Eq. 8.2, arrow 1.6, inductive (charge-migration McLafferty)"
      },
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "Charge-migration branch: the charge is carried away on the olefin, giving the propene radical cation C3H6+. (m/z 42, 2%) plus the neutral acetone enol CH2=C(OH)CH3 (-1.8). Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.2 is a thermochemical fragmentation map (log k printed above each reaction arrow, heats of formation printed below each species), not a curved-arrow figure. All electron moves here are curator-inferred from the mechanism-type label printed under the reaction arrow; none is drawn on the page. TWO double-barbed (heterolytic) arrows: move<1> the whole beta C3-C4 sigma pair becomes the new C4=C5 pi bond; move<2> the C5=O6 pi pair collapses onto O6 as a lone pair, neutralising O+ to the neutral enol oxygen. C3 is thereby stripped of its bonding electrons and becomes the propene cation centre while the odd electron stays on C2 -- encoded as the localised CH3-CH(.)-CH2+ form of propene+. (its C2=C3 alkene resonance partner is the same ion)."
    },
